342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (Q: Does NU have Erasmus+ agreements?)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (A: Yes, NU has numerous agreements for Student Mobility programs within the framework of the Erasmus program.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (Q: Can students find and participate in mobility programs on their own?)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (A: Yes, NU students can participate in Student Mobility programs on their own. However, the respective NU School still has to approve the program as credit-bearing. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (Q: Who announces mobility opportunities?)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (A: Each School announces exchange opportunities via email with all the requirements and set deadlines. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (Q: How long do student mobility programs usually last?)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (A: The most common period of academic exchange for most students is one semester. However, the duration of student mobility programs can vary, ranging from a few weeks to a full academic year.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
