354 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (Q: Are mobility programs free for NU students?)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
355 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (A: Mobility opportunities provided by NU based on NU cooperation links usually include Tuition fee waiver. Other expenses \(2-way air fare, accommodation, food expenses/costs, visa fee, medical insurance, miscellaneous expenses and additional university fees\) are covered by the student. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
356 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (Q: What are possible challenges along the student mobility program?)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (A: Challenges can include cultural adjustment, language barriers, homesickness, differences in educational systems, administrative complexities related to visa and travel regulations, and financial differences for living expenses.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (Q: Can I participate in academic mobility if I have a family or dependents?)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (A: There are no restrictions for students with families or dependents. However, visa issues and all the costs for their expenses should be borne by students.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (Q: Do I need to know the local language to participate in an academic mobility program?)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
361 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (A: Many courses at Host Institutions are usually offered in English, while some of them might require proficiency in the local language. Always check the language requirements of the specific program/course you're interested in.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
